{
  "$comment": [
    "Speech assets that ship in Resources/speech/ (ADR-0094, ADR-0095): the sherpa-onnx and ONNX Runtime shared libraries (no-TTS builds, so no espeak-ng), the X-ASR-zh-en 480 ms INT8 streaming model and the Silero VAD model.",
    "scripts/dev/fetch-speech-assets.mjs downloads each archive or file into .tools/cache/speech/, checks size and SHA-256 against this file, extracts only the members listed under `files`, checks every extracted file again and lays them out in target/speech-assets/<platform>-<arch>/ (the `to` paths). Nothing is downloaded or packaged without an entry here.",
    "Archive SHA-256 values match the `digest` that GitHub reports for each release asset; the file entries were computed from the extracted archives on 2026-11-26. `derived.bpe.vocab` is exported from bpe.model by scripts/dev/fetch-speech-assets.mjs (sentencepiece pieces and scores, the format sherpa-onnx reads for hotwords) and must hash to the value below.",
    "testFiles are real-speech WAVs from the model release, used by the real-model tests only and never packaged.",
    "Bumping a version: update the archive and every file entry together, run `node scripts/dev/fetch-speech-assets.mjs --all`, regenerate crates/piarc-sherpa-sys when the sherpa-onnx version changes (scripts/dev/gen-sherpa-sys.mjs) and update third-party/sources.json."
  ],
